From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koalabuttz <27229333+koalabuttz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 04:21:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: test the whole canonical field id in debugger
 compilation

EmitCanonicalString stores a 16-bit id at codePos and then tested only
its first byte, so a known field whose id has a zero low byte (256,
512, ...) was reported as "unknown field".

Test the 16-bit value that was stored.
---
 src/script/scr_compiler2.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/script/scr_compiler2.cpp b/src/script/scr_compiler2.cpp
index a1f4b718..271908c2 100644
--- a/src/script/scr_compiler2.cpp
+++ b/src/script/scr_compiler2.cpp
@@ -1097,7 +1097,7 @@ void EmitCanonicalString(uint32_t stringValue)
 	else if (scrCompilePub.developer_statement == SCR_DEV_EVALUATE)
 	{
 		*(unsigned short*)scrCompileGlob.codePos = Scr_CompileCanonicalString(stringValue);
-		if (!*scrCompileGlob.codePos)
+		if (!*(unsigned short *)scrCompileGlob.codePos)
 			CompileError(0, "unknown field");
 	}
 	else
